Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Curve 3: boundary for direct impact accretion with completely inefficient \
spin coupling, i.e. where all AM in accretion stream is lost / AM sink)\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.885417037435679*^9, 3.8854170632205887`*^9}, {
  3.986541086242836*^9, 3.986541118007667*^9}, {3.986542563555962*^9, 
  3.986542582796742*^9}, {3.9865428979519997`*^9, 3.986542908182996*^9}, {
  3.986543757367134*^9, 3.986543759941989*^9}, {3.98685799863028*^9, 
  3.986858031344447*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7bec4be7-e289-40e8-8fa2-\
4f1e4d8dcdba"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here, the extreme where all AM associated with the accretion stream is \
lost. In the usual stability criteria (Eq 4.) which is then used in Eq.3, an \
additional sink appears leading to Eq. 7.\n\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["R", "h"], "/", "a"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "b5cc9d35-df7c-4745-86ca-2267dfec5a38"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["r", "h"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "58fbc7ba-3414-4348-880d-1f235e45fb81"],
 " is the radius of the ring orbiting the accreting star. For an expression \
for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["r", "h"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c2f10b4-d2e3-4d1e-a7ec-2673c97a9dfb"],
 " , we take  Verbunt & Rappaport (1988)\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Equation 13. This \
comes from a fit to Lubow and Shu (1975) for mass ratios of order unity,  but \
Hut and Paczynski (1984) did this for more extreme mass ratios. \n(See \
discussion about Eq. 7 . for it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s origin re: angular \
momentum loss.)\n\n",
